    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d505">

                <pb facs="0988" n="976" sameAs="frus:frus1946v09/pg976"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Marshall Mission Files, Lot 54–D270:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">General Hsu Yung-chang to General Hsiung Shih-hui, at
                        Mukden</hi><anchor n="94" xml:id="d505-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Nanking</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-06-05">5 June 1946</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The Executive Headquarters, Peiping, will establish a branch office in Changchun.
                    Pending further instructions, that office shall then start functioning. In the
                    preparatory period you should render every assistance and convenience to the
                    said office.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d505-f1" n="94" type="source" xml:id="d505-f1-content">
                <p>Copy transmitted to General Marshall by Brig. Gen. Peter T. K. Pee, personal aide
                    to Generalissimo Chiang Kai-shek.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
